1. Vendored OOLONG scoring code

   File:     bench/oolong/vendor/oolong_eval_helpers.py
   Origin:   https://github.com/abertsch72/oolong, path src/eval/eval_helpers.py,
             commit 0bb7eabe839218fee7fe8d007f41cfc2fd3ae24c
   License:  MIT, Copyright (c) 2025 Amanda Bertsch
             (full text in bench/oolong/vendor/LICENSE.oolong)
   sha256:   247583a3b653b91c39fb88a102460802f1493175b23d05a7217aead0d685c64c

   The file is a byte-identical copy so that ASSAY's OOLONG scores are
   computed by the benchmark's own code. It is loaded through
   bench/oolong/scorer.py with its heavy dependencies stubbed. It is not
   modified. bench/oolong/vendor/PROVENANCE.md records the pin.

2. OOLONG corpus packs

   Files:    bench/oolong/packs/corpus_*.txt, questions_*.jsonl, manifest_*.json
   Origin:   derived from the OOLONG dataset at the revision pinned in each
             pack's manifest, by bench/oolong/packs/build_pack.py.
   Terms:    the dataset's own terms apply to the text (see the upstream
             dataset card named in the manifests). These files are not covered
             by the PolyForm license above.

   TODO(owner: O3): whether the packs ship in the repository (14 MB of
   upstream dataset text, with lines that look like personal data) or only
   the two smoke packs (spam4k, spam8k) and the manifests, with the rest
   fetched on first use through build_pack.py. The release review
